{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"Makefile","reason":"Add the amend-msg target that carries the existing Change-Id trailer forward."},{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"Name make amend-msg as the documented path for a rewritten commit message and warn that --amend -m/-F drop the Change-Id."},{"path":"scripts/amend_commit_message.py","reason":"The wrapper itself: the plan allows a thin script when the Makefile recipe gets unwieldy, and reading HEAD Change-Id + stripping a stray one from FILE + interpret-trailers placement is past what a make recipe should carry."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_amend_msg_change_id.py","reason":"Proves AC1 and AC2 together: the wrapper preserves the Change-Id AND, on the same fixture rewound to the same commit, naive git commit --amend -F loses it."}]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1787197866081305001,"uuid":"05d15482-4999-47fe-8342-e686f397cfcd"}